# A compiled Nim program has no extension on POSIX, which is what the first
# three lines are for: everything without a dot is ignored, so the test
# binaries and the editor itself stay out without being listed one by one.
*
!*/
!*.*
!LICENSE
nimcache/
nimblecache/
htmldocs/
testArtifacts/
staging/
/focim
# `nim c src/focim.nim` cannot write `src/focim` -- the directory of that
# name is already there -- so Nim writes `src/focim.out` instead, dot and all.
/src/focim.out
/deps
/nim.cfg
nimble.develop
nimble.paths
nimbledeps
